---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import Text from "@components/core/Text.astro"
import { Pages } from "@utils"
import PartnerFooter from "@components/PartnerFooter.astro"
---

<Layout title="Tennibot vs. Hydrogen | Tennibot" showFooter={false} showHeader={false} showPartnerHeader={true} showSecondaryHeader={false} showSecondaryMenu={false}>
    <main class="bg-t-off-black overflow-hidden text-t-off-white" >
        <section class="w-[80%] mx-auto mt-36 mb-24" >
            <Text tag="h1" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-center md:text-4xl text-2xl mb-10" >Tennibot Partner vs. Hydrogen Proton: What You Need to Know</Text>
        </section>

        <section class="w-[80%] mx-auto" >
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                When it comes to tennis ball machines, ultra-light doesn’t always mean ultra-smart.
                <br /><br />Here’s what you need to know before choosing between the Hydrogen Proton and the Tennibot Partner.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                1. Mobility vs. Portability: Which One Actually Saves You Time?
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Yes, the Hydrogen Proton is light and easy to carry. But once it’s on court, it stays put.
                <br />If you want to practice a wide range of shots—down-the-line, inside-out, cross-court—you’ll need to manually move the machine, adjust the angle, and reprogram the speed and spin every time.
                <br /><br />Tennibot Partner? Fully autonomous. It drives itself to the perfect position, creating realistic shot sequences with zero court-side hassle. You save energy for hitting—not setup.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                2. Intelligent Vision vs. No Awareness
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Hydrogen Proton doesn’t have any vision system. No cameras. No court mapping. No player detection. It simply fires balls in a fixed pattern with no awareness of what’s happening around it.
                <br /><br />
                Tennibot Partner features a synchronized, multi-camera vision system that sees the full court—including lines, net, player positioning, and lighting conditions. It’s powered by advanced algorithms built specifically for tennis, delivering dynamic, adaptive drills you can’t get from a stationary launcher.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                3. Shot Variety Without the Work
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Hydrogen Proton can deliver a basic set of drills, but only within the fixed physical limits of its setup—and without any knowledge of the player’s position or movement.
                <br /><br />Tennibot Partner’s combination of vision and mobility enables shot combinations that mimic real match play: forehand-to-backhand transitions, lateral sprints, and deep corner work—all customized via mobile app.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                4. Built for Players Who Want to Improve, Not Just Hit
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Hydrogen Proton is a fun tool if you’re looking for lightweight, recreational use or casual ball hitting.
                <br /><br />Tennibot is designed for players who want progression, intensity, and a smarter way to train. From USTA coaches to junior competitors, it’s trusted by athletes who treat practice like performance.
            </Text>

            <Text tag="h3" className="font-avenirBold text-t-green text-xl mb-10" >
                Final Thoughts
            </Text>
            <Text tag="p" className="font-plutoLight text-t-off-white text-base mb-10" >
                Hydrogen Proton is portable—but Tennibot Partner is powerful.
                <br /><br />If your goal is fun, light hitting, and compact gear, Proton delivers. But if you’re serious about performance, training quality, and intelligent features that actually improve your game—<span class="font-avenirBold text-t-green" >Tennibot Partner is the clear choice</span>.
            </Text>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>
<PartnerFooter />